Unless I'm missing something, I don't believe this will work. The issue is that when initializing a `struct gpio_pin_gaps` at compile time, the compiler would expect a definition like the following:
```
struct gpio_pin_gaps mcux_igpio_pin_gaps##n[] = {
   {
       3, /* start index */
       1, /* length */
   },
   {
       5, /* start index */
       4, /* length */
   },
}
```

However, the `DT_INST_PROP_OR` will expand to the following:
```
{3, 1, 4, 5}
```
This works fine to initialize an array of `uint8_t`, but for the `struct gpio_pin_gaps` it seems to generate a compiler warning: 

```
/home/danieldegrasse/zephyrproject/zephyr/build/zephyr/include/generated/devicetree_generated.h:6854:59: warning: missing braces around initializer [-Wmissing-braces]
 6854 | #define DT_N_S_soc_S_gpio_400c0000_P_gpio_reserved_ranges {0 /* 0x0 */, 1 /* 0x1 */}
````
